<title>UK: Aluminium stocks rose in December - IPAI.</title>
<headline>Aluminium stocks rose in December - IPAI.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total stocks of all forms of aluminium at Western world smelters excluding finished end-products, rose to 3.138 million tonnes at the end of December 1996, compared with the upwardly revised 3.093 million in November and 3.567 million in December 1995, provisional International Primary Aluminium Institute (IPAI) figures show.</p>
<p>Unwrought metal stocks rose to 1.691 million tonnes versus the upwardly revised 1.655 million and 1.996 million, respectively. </p>
<p>The regional breakdown of the total aluminium stocks was as follows, in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>			    Dec 96   Nov 96    Dec 95</p>
<p>    Africa		    71	 63	104</p>
<p>    North America	 1460     1455	1609</p>
<p>    Latin America	  158	174	 184</p>
<p>    East/South Asia	173	174	 158</p>
<p>    Europe		  1139     1085	1349</p>
<p>    Oceania		  137	142	 163</p>
<p>Unwrought metal stocks were distributed as follows, in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>			    Dec 96   Nov 96    Dec 95</p>
<p>    Africa		    24	 18	  51</p>
<p>    North America	  673	662	 785</p>
<p>    Latin America	  110	128	 144</p>
<p>    East/South Asia	143	150	 133</p>
<p>    Europe		   638	591	 767</p>
<p>    Oceania		  103	106	 116</p>
</text>
